{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And I will make your cities a desolation.</b> Meaning — they will not be settled even as other cities of the nations are, and this is a great anguish of spirit. This too declares beyond measure the annihilation of hope, as it says ״צִיּוֹן מִדְבָּר הָיָה״ and so forth (Isaiah 64:9), all the while that Israel does not mend their ways." "<b>And I will make desolate, etc.</b> Meaning — the resting of impurity and the establishment of its dwelling in the Temple, for the kelippah is called desolation (shimmamon), and the mystics have already made known that there the sedaemon rested and the heel of ס״מ trampled upon the House of YHWH — concerning this the heart is torn and the soul of every living being yearns toward the Master of the Palace." "<b>And I will not savor, etc.</b> Meaning — that He will not be pleased with their good deeds, so that even they might be attributed a pleasing fragrance (rei'ach ni'cho'ach); and similarly Jeremiah said (Lamentations 3:8): ״שָׂתַם תְּפִלָּתִי״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:02:30.418748606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}